wifi: iwlwifi: mvm: take a country learned while still on the world domain

Under location-aware regulatory (LAR) the firmware learns its country
from the access points it hears and reports it in MCC_CHUB_UPDATE_CMD.
iwl_mvm_rx_chub_update_mcc() drops every such report while an interface
is associated, so a country can't change under a live connection.

On the Surface Laptop 4 (AMD), whose AX200 takes no country from the
BIOS, the card associates 2.9 s after cfg80211 loads, before the
firmware has reported a country. Every report after that is
dropped, so the phy stays on the world domain (00) for as long as it
stays connected, which from boot is always. Disconnecting by hand and
scanning set the access point's country within 2 s, and the card kept
it after joining again.

Take the report while associated when the current domain is still the
world one. Leaving the world domain for the country the access point
itself announces keeps the channel it serves allowed; once the device
has a country, reports while associated are still ignored as before.

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/intel/iwlwifi/mvm/nvm.c b/drivers/net/wireless/intel/iwlwifi/mvm/nvm.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/intel/iwlwifi/mvm/nvm.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/intel/iwlwifi/mvm/nvm.c
@@ -617,6 +617,23 @@
 	return retval;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Whether the device still runs on the world regulatory domain, having never
+ * learned a country.
+ */
+static bool iwl_mvm_regdom_is_world(struct iwl_mvm *mvm)
+{
+	const struct ieee80211_regdomain *regd;
+	bool world;
+
+	rcu_read_lock();
+	regd = rcu_dereference(mvm->hw->wiphy->regd);
+	world = !regd || (regd->alpha2[0] == '0' && regd->alpha2[1] == '0');
+	rcu_read_unlock();
+
+	return world;
+}
+
 void iwl_mvm_rx_chub_update_mcc(struct iwl_mvm *mvm,
 				struct iwl_rx_cmd_buffer *rxb)
 {
@@ -630,7 +647,15 @@
 
 	lockdep_assert_held(&mvm->mutex);
 
-	if (iwl_mvm_is_vif_assoc(mvm) && notif->source_id == MCC_SOURCE_WIFI) {
+	/*
+	 * A country learned while associated is applied only when it replaces
+	 * the world domain. A device that associates before its first scan
+	 * reports a country would otherwise stay on the world domain for as
+	 * long as it stays connected, and the access point's own country
+	 * allows the channel it serves.
+	 */
+	if (iwl_mvm_is_vif_assoc(mvm) && notif->source_id == MCC_SOURCE_WIFI &&
+	    !iwl_mvm_regdom_is_world(mvm)) {
 		IWL_DEBUG_LAR(mvm, "Ignore mcc update while associated\n");
 		return;
 	}
